    {
      "id": "u_43493432fe5ea3b2433b7f42_0",
      "kind": "h2",
      "source": "Superscript, subscript__TRILIUM_PH_0__",
      "sourceHash": "43493432fe5ea3b2433b7f42a45c686978d36adb2919f870d168a71783352ada",
      "context": "General formatting > Superscript, subscript",
      "contextHash": "ccdf944d5df29816013f9a387506ab968780fb5b621d48b4d2e33c4a8a168f37",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_953d738bbf07b4d0963f5a15_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "This allows writing superscript or subscript text.",
      "sourceHash": "953d738bbf07b4d0963f5a1542d8b968581573ab5276466e52f2e96da5afacad",
      "context": "General formatting > Superscript, subscript",
      "contextHash": "ccdf944d5df29816013f9a387506ab968780fb5b621d48b4d2e33c4a8a168f37",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_74e3d05afa8f8debc6dfa805_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "This is mostly useful for units of measure (e.g. cm3 for cubic centimeters) and chemical notations (e.g. NaHCO3)",
      "sourceHash": "74e3d05afa8f8debc6dfa8053f81a0b5165925e70a333a8344d0a55e21ed4fa1",
      "context": "General formatting > Superscript, subscript",
      "contextHash": "ccdf944d5df29816013f9a387506ab968780fb5b621d48b4d2e33c4a8a168f37",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_eda27c5df825416ce7da181e_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "For mathematical formulas, prefer the __TRILIUM_PH_0__Math Equations__TRILIUM_PH_1__ feature instead.",
      "sourceHash": "eda27c5df825416ce7da181ee74f198fdbba4478e8edc424d8c50766c6632f00",
      "context": "General formatting > Superscript, subscript",
      "contextHash": "ccdf944d5df29816013f9a387506ab968780fb5b621d48b4d2e33c4a8a168f37",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_74954c2359eddb5604b42363_0",
      "kind": "h2",
      "source": "Font color and background color__TRILIUM_PH_0__",
      "sourceHash": "74954c2359eddb5604b42363fd649834b492ea9c372b4ca8312422b7c38b3ee2",
      "context": "General formatting > Font color and background color",
      "contextHash": "2a6bf631edb7686e3f2cb5da813f13e85254933043f7b8ae6c1109b8d4b3b51f",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_25fd4e81a8b26dffd0aaaee4_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Selected text can be colored with one of the predefined colors from a palette or any color can be selected using the color picker (__TRILIUM_PH_0__).",
      "sourceHash": "25fd4e81a8b26dffd0aaaee437877445d3759d27d1bec1bcb8096d75b342d040",
      "context": "General formatting > Font color and background color",
      "contextHash": "2a6bf631edb7686e3f2cb5da813f13e85254933043f7b8ae6c1109b8d4b3b51f",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_da034356e99abcf6dd45bf6b_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Once there is at least one color defined in the document, it will appear in the list for easy reuse.",
      "sourceHash": "da034356e99abcf6dd45bf6bca9033b47039d60a4a5bc80071cccf21482e9100",
      "context": "General formatting > Font color and background color",
      "contextHash": "2a6bf631edb7686e3f2cb5da813f13e85254933043f7b8ae6c1109b8d4b3b51f",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_476d87c86a25997538b607a9_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Colors adapt to the __TRILIUM_PH_0__theme__TRILIUM_PH_1__. Trilium shows each color in a lighter or darker shade that suits the current theme, so the text stays readable after switching between light and dark themes. The hue stays the same: red text is red in both themes, only lighter or darker. This applies to the palette, the color picker and the document colors alike, and to shared notes too. The swatches of the font color and background color dropdowns show the same shades on a sample text, \"Ab\": as the color of the text, or as the background behind it. Printed notes and PDF exports always use the shades of light themes, which suit white paper. The note itself keeps the color as it was picked, so an exported note shows it unchanged.",
      "sourceHash": "476d87c86a25997538b607a9940bc8a9846300169b64f7db292ee1ce2c47f9a9",
      "context": "General formatting > Font color and background color",
      "contextHash": "2a6bf631edb7686e3f2cb5da813f13e85254933043f7b8ae6c1109b8d4b3b51f",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_456086078f390802d01b0d76_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Colors applied with older versions of Trilium are shown exactly as they were picked, until the note is next edited.",
      "sourceHash": "456086078f390802d01b0d760efe72e782ab8dde4d0d8f61a47e2f03edd5421b",
      "context": "General formatting > Font color and background color",
      "contextHash": "2a6bf631edb7686e3f2cb5da813f13e85254933043f7b8ae6c1109b8d4b3b51f",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_e5a6d9d8c847faf011c92d6f_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Older browsers that can't adapt colors show them exactly as they were picked.",
      "sourceHash": "e5a6d9d8c847faf011c92d6f325e4dadfb8a7398f44585aa39c90cad6e71346d",
      "context": "General formatting > Font color and background color",
      "contextHash": "2a6bf631edb7686e3f2cb5da813f13e85254933043f7b8ae6c1109b8d4b3b51f",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_5aa9ca9a83627d41057abb78_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "When you paste text copied from a web page in Chrome, Edge or a Chromium-based app (such as Visual Studio Code), Trilium removes the page's styling:",
      "sourceHash": "5aa9ca9a83627d41057abb78b3453673578ac86e52f3f975a84923cc672cc876",
